pd.cut() in Pandas

pd.cut() is used to divide continuous numerical data into ranges (bins) and assign each value to a category.
                                                          -------


Simple meaning

pd.cut() converts numbers into groups/ranges.

For example, instead of having:

Age
22
27
35
42
58

you can create age groups:

18–30
31–40
41–50
51–60

====

1. Basic Example
import pandas as pd

ages = [22, 27, 35, 42, 58]

bins = [18, 30, 40, 50, 60]

result = pd.cut(ages, bins=bins)

print(result)

Output:

(18, 30]
(18, 30]
(30, 40]
(40, 50]
(50, 60]

Here:

18–30  → Young
31–40  → Middle
41–50  → Senior
51–60  → Older

====

2. Giving Meaningful Labels

Usually, we don't want (18, 30]. We want meaningful names.

ages = [22, 27, 35, 42, 58]

bins = [18, 30, 40, 50, 60]

labels = ["Young", "Adult", "Senior", "Older"]

result = pd.cut(
    ages,
    bins=bins,
    labels=labels
)

print(result)

===

Output:

Young
Young
Adult
Senior
Older

=====
